# PenguScript manual declaration binding for the PenguScript-friendly
# tomlc17 shim (pengu_tomlc17.h / wrappers_tomlc17.c, in libtomlc17.a).
# tomlc17: https://github.com/cktan/tomlc17 (MIT).
#
# This is a declaration file (.d.pengu): it only declares the native C
# surface so the LSP and the semantic checker know how to call the shim
# from PenguScript. The real C declarations live in `pengu_tomlc17.h`,
# which is `include`d below, so nothing here emits C code.
#
# Memory ownership: the shim only borrows its text/path argument and returns an
# int result, so no handle is returned and nothing here needs releasing.
#
# Why a shim: tomlc17's own API (toml_parse/toml_parse_file) returns the
# toml_result_t struct BY VALUE and hangs the parsed document off it as a
# toml_datum_t tree - by-value opaque structs cannot be expressed from
# PenguScript today. The shim reduces the parser to its smallest real,
# verifiable surface:
#   - pengu_toml_valid(text)      1 when `text` parses as valid TOML
#   - pengu_toml_valid_file(path) 1 when the file parses as valid TOML
# Querying keys/values from a parsed document remains C-level only.
#
# Type mapping notes:
#   - The text/path argument is a C string: declared `ref to char`. Pass a
#     PenguScript string literal directly, or a runtime string variable via
#     `bytes of <string>`.
#   - Return is an `int` (1 = valid, 0 = invalid/unreadable).
#
# Link requirement: -ltomlc17 (the shim object lives inside libtomlc17.a).
#
# Typical usage:
#   import std.tomlum
#   var ok as int is calling tomlum.pengu_toml_valid with "name = \"Pengu\""

include "pengu_tomlc17.h"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Functions (real C symbol names used verbatim - no insignia)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Returns 1 when `text` is a valid TOML document, 0 otherwise.
declare pengu_toml_valid with text as ref to frozen char into int

# Returns 1 when the file at `fname` is a valid TOML document,
# 0 otherwise (unreadable file or parse error).
declare pengu_toml_valid_file with fname as ref to frozen char into int